<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valdas Adamkus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1926</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valdas Adamkus is a Lithuanian-American environmental official and politician who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1998 to 2003 and from 2004 to 2009. Having emigrated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, he worked for the US Environmental Protection Agency before returning to Lithuania. His presidencies saw Lithuania invited into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>, both of which it joined in 2004.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valdas-adamkus.jpg" alt="Valdas Adamkus" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blowwhite · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valdas_Adamkus_portretas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
